The objective of this paper is not to provide an exhaustive or systematic survey of all RIS-VLC studies. Instead, it is to provide a topical review of RIS architectures applied to VLC technology, with emphasis on MS, MA, LC and STAR-RIS designs. More specifically, it provides a unified architectural analysis of key advances, limitations to application of RIS to enhance VLC transmission. It examines emerging technologies, explores potential future research directions, and presents a comparative analysis of several proposed solutions and approaches.

The research approach outlined here is a structured literature search to identify, collect, and analyze key studies related to the application of RIS in VLC, ultimately contributing to a better understanding of this emerging field. The paper main contributions are:

• Presents a unified taxonomy architectural analysis of RIS fundamentals and the diverse methodologies for their implementation in VLC systems;

• Compares RIS-VLC application scenarios and solutions reported in the literature;

• Presents a limitation of the analyzed studies;

• Presents the challenges and the road ahead for the technology to become useful on the next network generation and possible path to future work.

